 help is paid and whether the arrangement can last.":["u170"],"copy|Food insecurity or medication costs can look like self-neglect or poor adherence.":["u171"],"copy|A home visit can reveal hazards and whether shops, transport or other services are accessible.":["u172"],"copy|In a nursing home, personal care and nutrition matter more than shopping or meal preparation.":["u241"],"copy|Hospital assessment should compare function with pre-illness baseline and recheck it as recovery proceeds.":["u174"],"copy|Hazzard 8e, pp. 118 and 124–126.":["u175"],"copy|Establish who helps with specific tasks, whether help is paid and who could assist during illness.":["u242"],"copy|Financial strain can present as nonadherence, weight loss or apparent neglect (p124).":["u243"],"copy|Make the next visit actionable.":["u176"],"copy|Ask about spiritual or personal priorities and a concrete goal such as bathing safely or returning to an activity.":["u177"],"copy|Discuss preferences for future care while the person can participate and revisit them as prognosis changes.":["u178"],"copy|Previsit information from patients and families and trained staff screening can free clinician time for follow-up.":["u179"],"copy|Video visits require equipment and adequate hearing, vision and cognition, sometimes with caregiver help.":["u180"],"copy|Arrange an in-person visit when a physical examination or subtle gait findings will determine management.":["u181"],"copy|126–128.":["u183"],"copy|Combine reported function with observed performance when useful.":["u245"],"copy|Function reflects disease in the context of environment and support (p123).":["u246"],"copy|Tumor stage and ability to undergo treatment answer different questions.":["u112"],"copy|An older man with lung cancer had fallen, been hospitalized and left his own home.":["u247"],"copy|Establish his previous and present function, cognition, mood, nutritional status, medication burden and support.":["u114"],"copy|Ask what outcomes he would accept.":["u115"],"copy|Findings can change the treatment choice or identify barriers that the team can address.":["u116"],"copy|Symptom treatment and family support can proceed alongside anticancer treatment.":["u117"],"copy|The chapter gives chemotherapy as an example of specialty adaptation.":["u118"],"copy|Current practice: Geriatric assessment before cancer therapy.":["u249"],"copy|ASCO recommends geriatric assessment to identify vulnerabilities in older adults receiving systemic cancer therapy.":["u250"],"copy|How to use comprehensive geriatric assessment.":["u121"],"copy|Select a patient whose needs can respond to an intervention.":["u122"],"copy|During the team discussion, identify problems that need action.":["u123"],"copy|Involve the patient and, where appropriate, a caregiver to set goals.":["u124"],"copy|Prioritize actions by expected benefit and urgency.":["u125"],"copy|A suspected delirium-provoking drug merits immediate review.":["u126"],"copy|Assign someone to carry out each recommendation and someone to monitor it.":["u127"],"copy|When progress stalls, ask which steps were feasible, reassess illness and motivation, revise the plan and follow the result.":["u128"],"copy|128–130.":["u130"],"copy|What the trials measured.":["u131"],"copy|In geriatric inpatient units more patients were living at home and fewer entered nursing homes at three to twelve months.":["u132"],"copy|In eight randomized trials of joint hip-fracture care, fewer patients left hospital needing a higher care level than before the fracture.":["u133"],"copy|The lower inpatient mortality trend was statistically inconclusive.":["u134"],"copy|One posthospital trial reduced readmissions without a demonstrable improvement in functional decline, acute-care visits or depression at 24 weeks.":["u135"],"copy|Outpatient studies had inconsistent results.":["u136"],"copy|Preventive home visits that included an examination showed benefit for function in some groups.":["u137"],"copy|130–131.":["u139"],"copy|מתי ואיך מפנים.":["u184"],"copy|נפילות חוזרות, ירידה חדשה בתפקוד שאין לה הסבר, ריבוי תרופות ואשפוזים חוזרים הם מצבים שבהם כדאי לשקול הערכה כוללנית.":["u185"],"copy|אפשר לקבל הפניה מרופאת המשפחה או מרופא המשפחה.":["u186"],"copy|השירות כלול בסל ובאחריות קופת החולים.":["u187"],"copy|לקראת הביקור מביאים סיכום רפואי ורשימת תרופות, תוצאות בדיקות עדכניות וסיכום הערכה קודמת אם יש.":["u188"],"copy|רצוי לצרף בן משפחה שמכיר את התפקוד ביום־יום.":["u189"],"copy|משרד הבריאות, ״ייעוץ רפואי גריאטרי״, 18.12.2023, הסעיפים ״הערכה גריאטרית מקיפה״, ״איך להתכונן״ ו״המלצות״.":["u190"],"copy|מה אמור לחזור לרופא המפנה.":["u191"],"copy|הצוות בודק תפקוד, קוגניציה, מצב רוח, מצב חברתי וצרכים רפואיים וסיעודיים.":["u192"],"copy|לפי הצורך משלבים אנשי מקצוע נוספים או בודקים את סביבת הבית.":["u193"],"copy|הגריאטר מסכם את הממצאים ואת ההמלצות, משתף את המטופל ומשפחתו ומתאם עם הרופא הראשוני.":["u194"],"copy|המעקב כולל בירור אילו המלצות יושמו בפועל.":["u195"],"copy|חוזר מנהל רפואה 12/2007, סעיפים 3.2, 4.3, 6–8.2 · משרד הבריאות, ״מה כוללת ההערכה״ ו״המלצות ההערכה הגריאטרית המקיפה״.":["u196"],"copy|June 2026 Q38 Grading functional dependence p124":["u253"],"copy|September 2024 Q92 Screening and life expectancy p119":["u254"],"copy|June 2023 Q50 Recognizing the chair-stand test p121":["u255"],"copy|June 2022 Q27 Assessment after cancer staging p128":["u256"]},"maxId":256}
